use web, std

# The search box on every API library page, compiled to WebAssembly.

Global `IDX byte[>..]` holds the text of `/api-library/search.tsv`. Struct `Row` holds six offset and length pairs into it, for the columns name, kind, module, url, desc and level, plus `pub_rank` bool, true when the level column is `pub`. Global `ROWS Row[>..]`. `col(r Row, i int) const byte[:]` returns column `i` of a row as a view of `IDX`.

Globals: `Q` and `RES` are the element handles of `lib-q` and `lib-results`. `LOADED` and `LOADING` are bools. `QUERY byte[>..]` is the lowercase query with outer spaces trimmed. `SHOWN int[>..]` is the row indexes on screen, best first. `SEL int` is the highlighted position in `SHOWN`, -1 for none. Tags are `TAG_INPUT = 1`, `TAG_FOCUS = 2`, `TAG_KEY = 3`, `TAG_DOCKEY = 4`, `TAG_CLICK = 5`, `TAG_INDEX = 7`.

`parse_index()` splits `IDX` into `ROWS`. Each line has six tab-separated columns, and other lines are skipped. It walks the bytes once without copying.

`lower_has(hay const byte[:], needle const byte[:]) int` returns the first position where lowercase `needle` occurs in `hay`, comparing ASCII case-insensitively, or -1. `lower_eq(a const byte[:], b const byte[:]) bool` is the same test for equality.

`score(r Row, q const byte[:]) int` ranks a row against the query, 0 meaning no match. Let `name` be column 0, and `short` be the part of `name` after the last `::`. An exact match of `name` or `short` scores 1000. `short` starting with the query scores 800, `name` starting with it scores 750. The query found inside `name` scores 600, plus 50 when it starts right after a `_`. Otherwise the query is split on spaces and every word must occur in `name`, module, or desc: a row with all words found scores 200 plus 40 for each word found in `name` plus 20 for each found in module. Shorter names score up to 30 more, as 30 minus the name length, not below 0. Rows with a nonzero score get 100 more when `pub_rank` is true and 60 more when their kind column is `guide`.

`render()` draws the results. An empty `QUERY` hides `RES` with the `hidden` attribute and clears `SHOWN`. While the index is not loaded it shows `<p class="lib-rn">Loading...</p>`. Otherwise it scores every row, keeps the 40 best in a small sorted array with ties broken by name length then index, and sets the inner HTML of `RES` in one call to `web::html`. Each result is `<a class="lib-r" href="URL"><b>NAME</b><em>KIND in MODULE</em><small>DESC</small></a>`, all values HTML-escaped, with `<small>` left out when desc is empty and with the first result given the extra class `sel`. `SEL` starts at 0. With no results it shows `<p class="lib-rn">Nothing matches. Try a shorter word.</p>` and sets `SEL` to -1. It removes the `hidden` attribute at the end.

`move_sel(by int)` moves `SEL` by `by`, wrapping around `SHOWN`, does nothing when `SHOWN` is empty, removes class `sel` from the old child of `RES` and adds it to the new one, using `web::child`, `web::cls` and `web::release`, and calls `web::scroll_into(child, false, false)`.

`load_index()` starts `web::fetch("/api-library/search.tsv", TAG_INDEX)` once, guarded by `LOADING`.

`export fn he_event(tag i32, kind i32)` handles events by tag.
- `TAG_FOCUS` calls `load_index()`, then `render()` when `QUERY` is not empty.
- `TAG_INPUT` reads `web::ev_value` into a temporary, stores its lowercased, trimmed form in `QUERY`, calls `load_index()` and `render()`.
- `TAG_INDEX` with kind `web::EV_FETCH` calls `web::fetch_take(web::ev_id(), IDX)`, runs `parse_index()`, sets `LOADED`, calls `render()`.
- `TAG_KEY` reads `web::ev_key`. `ArrowDown` and `ArrowUp` call `web::ev_prevent()` and `move_sel(1)` or `move_sel(-1)`. `Enter` calls `web::ev_prevent()` and, when `SEL >= 0`, `web::navigate` to the url of `SHOWN[SEL]`, then sets the `hidden` attribute on `RES`. `Escape` sets the `hidden` attribute on `RES` and calls `web::call(Q, "blur")`.
- `TAG_DOCKEY` reads `web::ev_key`. On `/`, it takes `web::ev_target()`, and when that element's `tagName` from `web::get_prop` is neither `INPUT` nor `TEXTAREA`, it calls `web::ev_prevent()` and `web::call(Q, "focus")`. It releases the handle.
- `TAG_CLICK` takes `web::ev_target()` and `web::closest(t, ".lib-search")`, sets the `hidden` attribute on `RES` when `closest` returned 0, and releases both handles when they are nonzero.

`main()` sets `Q = web::el("lib-q")` and `RES = web::el("lib-results")` and returns when either is 0. Otherwise it listens with `web::listen` on `Q` for `input` with `TAG_INPUT`, `focus` with `TAG_FOCUS` and `keydown` with `TAG_KEY`, and on `web::DOCUMENT` for `keydown` with `TAG_DOCKEY` and `click` with `TAG_CLICK`, flags 0. Finally it reads the `value` property of `Q` with `web::get_prop`, because someone may have typed before the program loaded: when it is not empty it stores its lowercased, trimmed form in `QUERY` and calls `load_index()` and `render()`.
